message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cross-Domain Numerical Consistency Checks for Baker's Geometric Constant pi_g"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: Wayne
date-released: 2026-07-12
version: "2.1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/baker-geometric-pi-verification"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/baker-geometric-pi-verification"
abstract: >-
  A synchronized numerical verification suite for Baker's algebraically
  constructed geometric constant pi_g. The oracle-free construction uses a
  certified cubic branch and a scale-3 Richardson table. Eight bounded or
  directly residualized cross-domain consistency checks pass at 120 decimal
  digits. The computations are corroborative and do not prove pi_g=pi.
keywords:
  - geometric pi
  - pi_g
  - constructive geometry
  - Richardson extrapolation
  - cubic root certification
  - numerical verification
  - reproducibility
  - high precision
license: proprietary
